A||||3||Phantom Rage||88 Duck Woes||||1||
Z||000000||Phantom Rage||09-09-2000||07:43 PM||||My duck has been running strong for quite some time; it doesn’t even leak oil.  A few days ago, just out of the blue something went wrong.  When I started her, no problems but then she cut off after a few seconds.  I can keep her running if I give her a little gas.  The problem goes away after a minute or so.  I also noticed that when I feathered the gas my oil pressure gauge fluctuated rather abruptly.  I revved her up to 4g and noticed my oil pressure skyrocket to 80psi.  This too went away after the motor warmed up a bit. <P>Could it be a bad oil pressure switch?  I’ve read in the archives that (at least for the V6) the ECM controls the fuel pump signal for the first 2 seconds and then it switches the job over to the oil pressure switch.  Is this true and if so does it also apply to the 4 cylinder?  <P>Please, I need some help here. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-10-2000||12:12 AM||||ECM control is about 5 sec on all Fiero just to pressurize the system. Then it runs off the Oil sender.<P>So, yes, you guessed correctly. Replace the oil pressure sender.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||09-10-2000||11:33 AM||||I hate to disagree with Ogre, but the ECM in my 84 controls the fuel pump the entire time the engine is running.  The car will start and run just fine with the oil pressure switch completely disconnected. Checked the system description in the 88 shop manual (factory, not Haynes), and the V-6 fuel pump is also ECM controlled with the oil pressure switch as a backup. High oil pressure when the engine is revved cold is fairly normal.  Sounds to me like maybe the idle air controller is stuck closed since the engine will run with the accelerator opened a little. Especially since the problem seems to go away when the engine is warmed up a little.<BR>Just noticed you have an 88 4 cylinder--the shop manual description is the same.<BR>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE<p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 09-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phantom Rage||09-10-2000||05:53 PM||||Thank You fella's <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I replaced both a while back.  They both have a life time warranty, so I guess I will repace both.||||reg||1
